ENTRY            41463   20150928   20151123   20151116       4171
SUBENT        41463001   20150928   20151123   20151116       4171
BIB                 16         31
TITLE       Measurement of thermal neutron radiative capture
            cross-sections of the 14-N And 19-F by in-beam
            gamma-spectroscopy method with reactor neutrons
AUTHOR     (A.I.Egorov,R.I.Krutova,Yu.E.Loginov,S.Eh.Malyutenkova)
INSTITUTE  (4RUSLIN)
REFERENCE  (J,NIM/A,545,296,2005)
FACILITY   (REAC,4RUSLIN) WWR-M Reactor
METHOD     (TOF) For neutron spectrum measuring.
           (GSPEC) Detection of prompt g-rays emitted following
            neutron capture and of photons accompanying beta decay
            of residual nuclei.
INC-SOURCE (REAC) External thermal neutron beam of WWR-M reactor.
INC-SPECT   Narrow neutron spectrum,maximum at 0.028+-0.002 eV,
            FWHM about 0.03 eV,most probable neutron velocity
            2200m/s. Neutron flux at sample site 2.E+7 n/cm2/s.
SAMPLE      Homogeneous mixture of chemical compounds
            Pb(NO3), CaF2, LiF and Teflon with Al2O3.
DETECTOR   (HPGE) Efficiency error <= 0.4% up to E-gamma 2 MeV.
MONITOR    ((MONIT)13-AL-27(N,G)13-AL-28,,SIG)
MONIT-REF  (,S.F.Mughabghab+,B,NEUT.CS 1A,,1981)
DECAY-MON  (13-AL-28,2.24MIN,DG,1779.,1.)
ANALYSIS          Comparison of areas of g-lines in isotope under
            investigation and in isotope used as standard.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total error (1.5-2.%)
           (ERR-1) Error of cross-section standards
           (ERR-2) Error of gamma-efficiency of spectrometer
           (ERR-3) Error of number of atoms determination
HISTORY    (20060208C)  Compiled at CJD (M.M.)
           (20150928A) M.M. AUTHOR and TITLE were corrected.
            NO-DIM -> PC/REAC for ASSUM (-ERR) values; REL deleted
            from ASSUMED reactions.
ENDBIB              31
COMMON               8          6
EN         EN-RSL-FW  ERR-1      ERR-2      ERR-3      MONIT
MONIT-ERR  EN-ERR
EV         EV         PER-CENT   PER-CENT   PER-CENT   B
B          EV
0.028      0.03       1.         0.5        0.1        0.231
0.003       0.002
ENDCOMMON            6
ENDSUBENT           41
ENDENTRY             1
